-| `image_sample_l` / `image_sample_lz` in every dimension | The T# FORMAT rule applies to a 2D-array, 3D, cube and 1D image too: the sample reads the uint/sint alias of that dimension's sampled binding (3, 6 and 5; a cube uses its 6-layer 2D-array view) and keeps the float view for a float format, the same `image_read_typed` dispatch `image_load` uses. Confirmed by `tests/semantic/test_sample_typed_dims.py` (the alias and sampled-image type each dimension emits, that a float format still samples the float view, and `spirv-val --target-env vulkan1.2`) and `runtime/src/vulkan_bindless.h` (`sampled_binding`). The format rule itself is the 2D row above; a GPU readback on a non-2D integer texture is not measured yet. |
