 | Barrier-round count in LDS (SHADER-579) | Barrier rounds (see "Workgroup barriers") count the invocations not done in `%x_buf`, three `Workgroup` dwords (#930). On a full 32 KiB LDS that made 32,780 B, 12 bytes over the 32,768 B `maxComputeSharedMemorySize` of the AMD Windows (RX 9070 XT) and Intel (UHD 770) drivers, so the runtime refused those pipelines (2 native wave32 cs in towade's 1.0.2.1 corpus, [finding](https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/pull/1882#issuecomment-7084298032)). Rule (`bar_counts_in_lds`): when the shader uses its LDS and the LDS array plus 12 bytes is over 16,384 B (the Vulkan minimum limit, so in practice an array of 16, 32 or 64 KiB), there is no `%x_buf`. The count borrows LDS word 0 at the end of each round (`bar_scheduler_tail`): after the round's barrier every invocation is done or waits at `s_barrier`, so no shader code runs; invocation 0 saves the word in a Function variable and clears it, barrier, every invocation not done adds 1 atomically, barrier, all read the count, barrier, invocation 0 stores the saved word back, barrier. The shader sees its LDS bit for bit as before, and the four extra barriers sit where the whole workgroup already waits, so `s_barrier`'s semantics are unchanged; the cost is four more `OpControlBarrier`s per round in those shaders only. Below the threshold `%x_buf` stays (12 bytes fit every device) with one barrier per round; a shader that never touches its LDS also keeps it (no array to borrow from, 12 B in all). A 32 KiB LDS is now exactly 32,768 B and a 64 KiB one 65,536 B (before: 65,548 B, refused or shrunk to its allocation). Not chosen: putting the count in LDS the shader never touches (unprovable with dynamic addresses), or deciding per device (the translator runs offline). Pinned by `tests/semantic/test_cs_barrier_counts_lds.py` (Workgroup bytes from the emitted SPIR-V and `lds_bytes` for 32 KiB, 64 KiB and small LDS, under a 32 KiB `--max-shared-memory`; ring shifts across 10 barriers that read word 0 and an early-ending wave in the workgroup interpreter, whose LDS starts as 0xDEADBEEF, in both wave orders). Confirmed by those CPU tests only; GPU runs on the 32 KiB devices are pending. |
-| LDS | A `Workgroup` uint array sized from LDS_SIZE, rounded up to a power of two that also covers every constant offset (15 of 486 shaders index past LDS_SIZE). Covers `ds_read/write_b32..b128`, `read2/write2` (+`st64`), `u16`/`i16`/`u8`/`i8` reads (also `ds_read_u16_d16`/`_d16_hi` and, since SHADER-85, `ds_read_u8_d16`/`_d16_hi` and `ds_read_i8_d16`/`_d16_hi`: the byte is zero- or sign-extended 8→16 into one half of the destination VGPR and the other half is kept, per the RDNA2 ISA DS opcode descriptions (opcodes 162–165) and as for the u16 d16 reads; GPU-checked with `cs_w32_lds_u8_d16.asm`, byte values 0x80/0xFF/0x7F with a non-zero `offset:`), `b16`/`b8` writes (atomic and/or, so neighbouring lanes don't race; a 16-bit read or write at byte 3 of a dword also reads or writes byte 0 of the next dword, as llc-15 `-mcpu=gfx1030 -mattr=+unaligned-access-mode` emits one `ds_read_u16`/`ds_write_b16 ... offset:3` for an align-1 halfword; until 2026-11-22 the reads extracted 16 bits at bit 24, undefined in SPIR-V, and the writes kept only byte 3; `tests/semantic/test_lds_u16_cross_dword.py`), the add/sub/min/max/and/or/xor atomics with and without return, `wrxchg`, `cmpst` (`OpAtomicCompareExchange` with DATA as comparator and DATA2 as value), and `ds_bpermute_b32` as a subgroup shuffle. GPU-checked with `cs_w32_lds_u8_d16.asm`, byte values 0x80/0xFF/0x7F with a non-zero `offset:`), `b16`/`b8` writes (atomic and/or, so neighbouring lanes don't race), the add/sub/min/max/and/or/xor atomics with and without return, `wrxchg`, `cmpst` (`OpAtomicCompareExchange` with DATA as comparator and DATA2 as value), and `ds_bpermute_b32` as a subgroup shuffle. `ds_permute_b32`, its forward (scatter) form, has no Vulkan equivalent: each source lane that is on in EXEC publishes `((vAddr + offset) >> 2) mod 32` and each destination lane scans the 32 sources of its half and keeps the last one that targets it (a shuffle of target and data per source lane; under `--wave64-emulate` two buffer rounds and a Function variable instead). Per the ISA pseudocode (`tmp[0..63] = 0`; `next if !EXEC[i]` on the source; `VGPR[VDST][i] = tmp[i]` only `if EXEC[i]`): a destination lane nobody targets gets 0, an off source sends nothing, an off destination keeps its VDST, and the half rule above applies as for `ds_bpermute_b32`. When several sources target one lane the ISA leaves the winner unpredictable ("the value from one of the writers"; its pseudocode says the highest-numbered); the translator takes the highest, and nothing may depend on it. Confirmed by the GPU tests `cs_w32_permute.asm` and, per half of a wave64, `cs_w64x_permute.asm` (SHADER-90: rotation, offset, unwritten lane = 0, off destination keeps its value, off source does not win), `cs_w32_partial_permute.asm` (a 20-thread wave32: a launched lane whose source lane was never launched gets 0, and a send to a missing lane is lost; the same words from a raw 20-thread `hw_oracle` kernel on `gfx1036`) and `tests/semantic/test_ds_permute.py`. **Hardware-verified on RDNA2 (`gfx1036`, AMD Ryzen 7 9800X3D iGPU, Linux AMDGPU DRM via `tools/hw_oracle`, wave32 and wave64, SHADER-133)** with `tools/ds_permute_probe.py` (9/9 cases exact in both wave sizes): unaddressed active lanes get 0, off destinations keep VDST, off sources send nothing, 2-/4-/32-way collisions deterministically take the highest-numbered active lane in the 32-lane half (matching the translator), `vAddr + offset` carries from the low 2 bits before `>> 2` mod 32, wave64 runs as two independent 32-lane halves (`+32` wraps within each half), and missing lanes of a partial wave (20 threads in wave32, 40 in wave64) send nothing. A source lane that is off in EXEC reads 0 and an off destination lane keeps its value (RDNA ISA §10.4.4), in wave32 as in wave64. In wave64 the permute also runs as two wave32s: each half reads lanes of its own half. Until 2026-11-21 lanes 32–63 of a 64-wide subgroup read the low half and inactive sources kept their value (`c