el, which are packed from lane 0 (a quad with no covered pixel isn't in the wave); lane % 4 = (x & 1) + 2 (y & 1), so lanes 0-3 are top-left, top-right, bottom-left, bottom-right; a helper's `v_interp` gives its own pixel centre (extrapolated, as precisely as a covered pixel), and its v0/v1 hold its own I/J before `s_wqm` too; without `s_wqm` its VGPRs aren't written; an `exp ... vm` with helpers on in EXEC writes no pixel outside the triangle. Not covered: helper-invocation behaviour at triangle edges is untested, and in native mode an absent invocation in a partial quad (a compute group whose size is not a multiple of 4) gives an undefined value (emulated, the missing lanes of a partial wave read as 0). Before this the instruction was the identity, so helper lanes stayed off (#156 SHADER-34: `s_wqm_b64` appears in 4,285 pixel shaders). GPU-checked with `runtime/test/shaders/cs_wqm_w64.asm`, `cs_wqm_w64_half.asm`, `cs_wqm_w32.asm` and `ps_wqm.asm` on AMD Radeon 880M (subgroup 64) and NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Laptop (subgroup 32; `cs_wqm_w64` there needs `LEONIDA_W64_EMULATE=1`), with and without `--wave64-emulate`. |
